irection":null,"citationId":"c26","passages":2},{"other":{"id":"edge","label":"edges"},"kind":"co_mention","relation":null,"direction":null,"citationId":"c27","passages":2}],"linksLeftOut":90,"claims":[{"citationId":"c1","pages":[{"id":"extract","label":"Extract"},{"id":"large_language_model","label":"open information extractors"},{"id":"triplet","label":"Triplet"}]}],"mentions":[{"citationId":"c28"},{"citationId":"c29"},{"citationId":"c30"},{"citationId":"c2"},{"citationId":"c6"},{"citationId":"c4"},{"citationId":"c31"},{"citationId":"c32"},{"citationId":"c33"},{"citationId":"c34"}],"mentionsLeftOut":101,"citations":[{"id":"c1","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_e69bc461a720c1b6","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":2,"quote":"the Extract subtask leverages recent findings that LLMs are effective open information extractors (Li et al., 2023; Han et al., 2023) — they can extract semantically correct and meaningful triplets."},{"id":"c2","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_d13a7a33d897ce11","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":8,"quote":"Data sum- maries are stored at each node, aiding in the swift traversal of data and assisting the RAG system in determining which chunks to extract."},{"id":"c3","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_c998a018b9aa2f1a","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":13,"quote":"Entity Extraction Prompt Given a piece of text, extract a list of enti- ties from it."},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_02012b4621581282","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":4,"quote":"3.1.2 Text Chunks →Entities & Relationships In this step, the LLM is prompted to extract instances of important entities and the relationships between the entities from a given chunk."},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_8240c2e11040036d","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":26,"quote":"Since the only concept tagged by HippoRAG is “protons”, it extracts passages related to “Uranium” and “nuclear weapons” while ColBERTv2 uses the context to extract more relevant passages associated with the discovery of atomic numbers."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"6c24762a3f277fd1_c_b111edc0d96e0395","docId":"6c24762a3f277fd1","docTitle":"2309.15217_Ragas_Automated_Evaluation_of_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":3,"quote":"To estimate faithfulness, we first use an LLM to extract a set of statements, S(as(q))."},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_b66d789a66166909","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":19,"quote":"• Traversal-based retriever: These methods traverse the graph and extract paths to aid in answering a specific question."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_283bc89c445357cb","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":2,"quote":"Open Information Extraction: extract a list of entity-relation triplets from the input text freely."},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_6f7bbe7480ca88cc","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":19,"quote":"[110] extract all paths of length k ≤2 between seed entities."},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_e2ab10a48622bc45","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":4,"quote":"We then add the named entities to the OpenIE prompt to extract the final triples, which also contain concepts (noun phrases) beyond named entities."},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"730f1a9f38d16689_c_e91cebec88d549b4","docId":"730f1a9f38d16689","docTitle":"2404.16130_From_Local_to_Global_A_Graph_RAG_Approach_to_Query_Focused_Summarizati","page":5,"quote":"The LLM can also be prompted to extract claims about detected entities."},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_cc8c385b6ddbc31f","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":1,"quote":"We demonstrate on three KGC benchmarks that EDC is able to extract high- quality triplets without any parameter tuning and with significantly larger schemas compared to prior works."},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_e2db5885908b04d1","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":9,"quote":"As seen in Table 7, both ColBERTv2 and IRCoT fail to extract the necessary passages since they cannot access these associations."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_ab4c9837b1bf7083","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":4,"quote":"Using our example above, the prompt is: OIE Prompt Given a piece of text, extract relational triplets in the form of [Subject, Relation, Object] from it."},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_04dddb1c2d05d742","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":25,"quote":"As further discussed in §F.2, our NER design does not extract enough information from the query for retrieval."},{"id":"c16","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_65376575c9d615eb","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":3,"quote":"Through few-shot prompt- ing, LLMs identify and extract relational triplets ([Subject, Relation, Object]) from input texts, inde- pendent of any specific schema."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_d14dde25bca9df65","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":8,"quote":"Experiments show that EDC and EDC+R are able to extract better KGs than specialized trained models when a tar- get schema is available and dynamically create a schema when none is provided."},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"6c24762a3f277fd1_c_d7742c667fe86e6a","docId":"6c24762a3f277fd1","docTitle":"2309.15217_Ragas_Automated_Evaluation_of_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation","page":4,"quote":"ntences, Sext, from c(q) that are crucial to answer q, using the following prompt: Please extract relevant sentences from the provided context that can potentially help answer the following question."},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_12d62c2ec5755b12","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":33,"quote":"• CADRO: The Common Alzheimer’s and Related Dementias Research Ontology (CADRO) 23 is employed to extract a subset of Alzheimer’s disease (AD)-related samples from the medical QA datasets for evaluation."},{"id":"c20","chunkId":"ac529ab762fd1672_c_c7b8924c28c2d6cd","docId":"ac529ab762fd1672","docTitle":"HybridRAG: Integrating Knowledge Graphs and Vector Retrieval Augmented Generation for Efficient Information Extraction","page":7,"quote":"In KG as the information is stored in the form of entities and relationships and there can be multiple relations emanating from one single entity, in this experiment, to extract relevant information from th"},{"id":"c21","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_e2ab10a48622bc45","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":4,"quote":"Specifically, we first extract a set of named entities from each passage."},{"id":"c22","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_b80a8a944ff88263","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":18,"quote":"This takes the form of custom parsers and manually defined rules used to extract facts from raw text."},{"id":"c23","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_9db3f68bd65133e5","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":3,"quote":"Given input text, our goal is to extract relational triplets in a canonical form such that the resulting KGs will have minimal ambiguity and redundancy."},{"id":"c24","chunkId":"14671c78fc7de99d_c_e4013d6b8b380f63","docId":"14671c78fc7de99d","docTitle":"2405.14831_HippoRAG_Neurobiologically_Inspired_Long_Term_Memory_for_Large_Languag","page":7,"quote":"To understand the relationship between OpenIE and retrieval performance more deeply, we extract 239 gold triples from 20 examples from the MuSiQue training set."},{"id":"c25","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_c6eddb182e6cc914","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":20,"quote":"• Subgraph-based retriever: These methods extract a subgraph of size k around each of the seed entities."},{"id":"c26","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_b1c04fb92334f523","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":20,"quote":"They further augment this by extracting the top k most similar questions in the dataset using BM25 [338], and extract the triples for each of them."},{"id":"c27","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_32a1ba5d5a858d6e","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":49,"quote":"For example, deciding on the granularity of nodes and edges, as well as which entities or relationships to extract, is critical."},{"id":"c28","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_6940e750d78fc24e","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","p